    "text": "To determine the total number of pieces of bread Sally eats across Saturday and Sunday, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of sandwiches Sally eats on Saturday.\n2. Calculate the number of sandwiches Sally eats on Sunday.\n3. Determine the total number of sandwiches Sally eats over the two days.\n4. Calculate the total number of pieces of bread used, knowing that each sandwich uses 2 pieces of bread.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. Sally eats 2 sandwiches on Saturday.\n2. Sally eats 1 sandwich on Sunday.\n3. The total number of sandwiches Sally eats over the two days is:\n   \\[\n   2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n4. Since each sandwich uses 2 pieces of bread, the total number of pieces of bread Sally eats is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 2 = 6\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of pieces of bread Sally eats across Saturday and Sunday is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
